# Where the *ValidationTest suite finds real statements to reconcile against.
#
# Copy this file to `statements.local.properties` (gitignored) and uncomment only the
# keys you actually have statements for. Every key is optional: an unset one makes its
# test skip, which is what happens on CI and on a fresh clone.
#
# EVERY KEY BELOW SHIPS COMMENTED OUT, deliberately. A key set to a path that does not
# exist is an error (see below), so a template with live placeholder paths would fail
# tests the moment you copied it — teaching you that this mechanism cries wolf, which is
# the one lesson that would stop you trusting it when it is right.
#
# USE FORWARD SLASHES. This is a java.util.Properties file, where backslash is the
# escape character: `C:\Users\me\statements` silently loads as `C:Usersmestatements`,
# and a backslash before a `u` — `C:\users\...` — is a malformed unicode escape that
# fails the whole file. Forward slashes work fine on Windows.
#
# THE KEYS BELOW ARE NOT A SCHEMA. LocalStatements resolves whatever key it is asked
# for; no name is special to it. Nothing here requires you to have a statement from any
# particular institution, or any statement at all — this repository ships no validation
# test, because it ships no parser for a real issuer. The one parser here reads a format
# that does not exist, so it can be demonstrated without anyone's data.
#
# Bringing your own is the expected path: write a parser, write a validation test, pick
# a key name, put the folder here. NorthwindStatementParser is the worked example, and
# the parts worth copying are that the parse is reconciled against whatever control
# totals the statement itself prints, and that it refuses rather than guesses.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: these paths used to be hard-coded in the test sources, which
# published a home directory, an account nickname, and the institutions behind each
# parser to anyone who read the repo. Statement PDFs were never committed; the paths
# to them effectively were. The parsers themselves have since moved out too.
#
# A SKIP IS NOT A PASS. If you have statements and the test skips, this file is wrong.
# A parser is only proven against real statements here — see README, "Testing".
#
# HOW EACH KEY BEHAVES
#   unset / blank / commented out  -> the test skips, quietly. Nothing was requested.
#   set and correct                -> the test runs.
#   set and pointing at nothing    -> the test FAILS, naming the key and the bad path.
#
# The third case is not a demand that the data exist forever — it is a demand that this
# file and your disk agree, and you can settle that from either side. If a folder moved,
# fix the path. If it is gone for good and you do not want it checked any more, blank the
# key or comment it out; it drops straight back to the first case and stays quiet. What is
# not available is leaving a wrong path in place and having it ignored, because that is
# indistinguishable from the tests still running.
#
# You can also set any key for one run without a file:
#   ./mvnw test -Dpigpurchases.statements.mycard=D:/statements/mycard
# or from the environment, upper-cased with dots as underscores:
#   PIGPURCHASES_STATEMENTS_MYCARD=/mnt/statements/mycard

# --- Your statement folders -----------------------------------------------------
# One key per folder of statements. The key name is yours to choose: a validation test
# asks LocalStatements for whatever key it was written with, and nothing here treats any
# name as special. These are examples of the shape, not a list to fill in.

# mybank.primary=C:/path/to/statements/mybank/2026
# mybank.business=C:/path/to/statements/mybank-business/2026
# mycard=C:/path/to/statements/mycard/2026

# --- A reference statement, if your validation test uses one ---------------------
# Naming one statement whose figures you have checked by eye gives a test its sharpest
# assertions: an exact count and an exact total. They describe YOUR statement, so they
# live here rather than in the test.
#
# Keys like these travel as a GROUP - set them all, or leave them all out. A
# half-configured reference reads as configured while asserting almost nothing, and is
# rejected rather than quietly checking less.

# mycard.sample.file=statement-2026-07-01.pdf
# mycard.sample.count=3
# mycard.sample.total=123.45
# mycard.sample.utilities=Sewer,Trash,Water
